E('space exploration|mars rover|curiosity rover|perseverance', 'Space exploration has sent robots across the solar system.', 'The first Mars landers touched down in the 1970s.', 'NASA’s Viking 1 landed on Mars in 1976.', 'Curiosity has explored Mars since 2012.', 'Perseverance landed in 2021, with a small helicopter, Ingenuity.', 'Ingenuity made the first powered flight on another planet.')
E('james webb|james webb space telescope|jwst', 'The James Webb Space Telescope is the most powerful space telescope ever built.', 'It launched on 25 December 2021.', 'It observes mainly in infrared light.', 'Its gold-coated mirror is 6.5 metres across.', 'It orbits the Sun about 1.5 million kilometres from Earth.', 'It can see some of the earliest galaxies.')
E('climate change|global warming', 'Climate change is the long-term warming of Earth, driven mainly by human activity.', 'Scientists warned about the greenhouse effect as early as the 19th century.', 'Burning fossil fuels releases carbon dioxide, which traps heat.', 'Earth has warmed by about 1.1 to 1.2 °C since pre-industrial times.', 'Effects include rising seas, heatwaves and melting ice.', 'The Paris Agreement of 2015 aims to limit warming to well below 2 °C.')
E('nuclear power', 'Nuclear power generates electricity by splitting atoms.', 'The first nuclear power plant to supply a grid opened in the Soviet Union in 1954.', 'It produces very little carbon dioxide.', 'Its waste stays radioactive for a very long time.', 'Major accidents include Chernobyl in 1986 and Fukushima in 2011.')
E('fukushima', 'The Fukushima disaster was a nuclear accident in Japan.', 'It began on 11 March 2011.', 'A huge earthquake and tsunami knocked out the plant’s cooling systems.', 'Three reactors suffered meltdowns.', 'The tsunami itself killed nearly 20,000 people.', 'Over 100,000 people were evacuated.')
E('olympics modern|modern olympics|pierre de coubertin', 'The modern Olympic Games were revived by Pierre de Coubertin.', 'The first modern Games were held in Athens in 1896.', 'The Winter Olympics began in 1924.', 'The five rings represent the five inhabited continents.', 'The Paralympics began in 1960.')
E('nato', 'NATO is a military alliance of North American and European countries.', 'It was founded on 4 April 1949.', 'Members promise to defend each other if attacked (Article 5).', 'Article 5 has been invoked only once, after the September 11 attacks.', 'It has over 30 members.')
E('google', 'Google is an American technology company best known for its search engine.', 'It was founded in 1998 by Larry Page and Sergey Brin.', 'They started it as Stanford University students.', 'Its name comes from “googol”, the number 1 followed by 100 zeros.', 'It became part of Alphabet in 2015.')
E('video games|first video game|pong', 'Video games grew from experiments into a giant global industry.', 'Pong, released in 1972, was one of the first commercially successful arcade games.', 'Early experiments include Tennis for Two in 1958.', 'Home consoles spread in the 1970s and 1980s.', 'Super Mario Bros. (1985) is one of the best-selling games ever.', 'Today the industry is larger than film and music combined.')
E('social media', 'Social media are online platforms for sharing and connecting.', 'They grew rapidly in the 2000s.', 'Early sites included Friendster and MySpace.', 'Facebook launched in 2004, YouTube in 2005 and Twitter in 2006.', 'Billions of people now use them daily.')
E('cars electric|electric cars', 'Electric cars run on batteries rather than petrol.', 'Electric cars existed in the 1890s, before petrol cars became dominant.', 'They faded as cheap petrol cars spread.', 'Modern electric cars took off in the 2010s.', 'Many countries plan to phase out new petrol cars.')
E('human genome project|genome', 'The Human Genome Project mapped the entire human genetic code.', 'It ran from 1990 to 2003.', 'It was an international effort.', 'Humans have about 20,000 protein-coding genes.', 'It transformed medicine and biology.')
E('dolly the sheep|cloning', 'Dolly the sheep was the first mammal cloned from an adult cell.', 'She was born on 5 July 1996, in Scotland.', 'She was created at the Roslin Institute.', 'She was named after the singer Dolly Parton.', 'She lived until 2003.')
E('large hadron collider|lhc|cern|higgs boson', 'The Large Hadron Collider is the world’s largest particle accelerator.', 'It began operating in 2008, at CERN near Geneva.', 'It is a 27-kilometre ring underground.', 'In 2012 it found the Higgs boson.', 'The Higgs gives other particles mass.', 'The World Wide Web was also invented at CERN.')
